WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.190
Phew!

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.690
Man, why is it so hot?

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.780
Well, look at it this way.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.400
For summer vegetables like tomatoes and cucumbers, this is far better than the cold.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.030
Tomatoes don't like cold?

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.070
Yeah.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:21.120
Low temperatures slow their growth and damage the fruit.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:21.870
Really?

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:23.710
What about soybeans?

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.290
Are soybeans okay with heat?

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.710
Yes, they should be fine.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:32.090
When we planted them, I mentioned their wide range of applications,

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:35.430
but soybeans have one power
that's greater than all the rest.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.090
Power?

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:41.310
Kousaku, why don't you tell her about
the three primary nutrients in agriculture?

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.430
Sure.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:43.180
They're as follows:

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.850
nitrogen, phosphoric acid, and potassium.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.110
Of the three, nitrogen is particularly important.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.030
Without it, plants can't grow at all.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:53.690
Nitrogen?

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:55.030
That's right.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:56.910
Soybeans' greatest power

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:00.030
is that they infuse
the soil with nitrogen.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.620
They take in molecular
nitrogen from the air

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.210
and convert them into
nitrogen compounds.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:09.330
In other words, they create their own fertilizer.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.550
Soybeans... are amazing.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:14.800
<i>July.</i>

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>The season of scorching sun was upon us.</i>

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.970
<i>Our agricultural school life
was about to heat up as well!</i>

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:52.770
All right!

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.190
Let's do our darndest today!

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:00.110
Wh-What's with all the food?

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.030
Cucumber, tomato, eggplant,
green pepper, bitter melon, okra,

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.330
Japanese ginger, pumpkin, zucchini, and corn!

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.080
We got heaps of the surplus vegetables!

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.990
And for free, to boot!

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:11.290
It's a rootin' tootin' buffet!

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.880
We agricultural students,
who learn the value of life and food,

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.800
have one golden rule.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.260
Which is?

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.520
There'd better not be no leftovers!

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:23.800
Don't forget!

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.510
You don't need to tell me twice!

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.720
Time to eat!

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.480
What's wrong, Hata?

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:37.020
Nakazawa made a ton of food
from the free veggies they got.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.190
I see.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.320
It's that time of year, isn't it?

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.030
Remember how crazy
the melon festival was last year?

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.070
It was like a never-ending harvest!

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:52.910
I see you're driveling away over your usual nonsense.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:54.900
Muskmelons!

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.720
No, Densuke watermelons!

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:03.090
I-I remember mailing some
of the melons to Ringo.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.140
Of course, I picked the sweetest ones.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.010
Yes, I know.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.810
Right, right.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.430
Wait, you know?

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.480
It's been a long day,

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.650
so y'all deserve this!

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:23.740
I-I guess having a bigger harvest than you know what to do with

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:25.740
is quite the first world problem.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:26.660
Darn tootin'!

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.990
Count yer blessin's as you eat!

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:30.580
Okay!

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.200
Time to eat!

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.090
Whoa!

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:35.330
Minori, this bitter melon
cold shabu is great!

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.540
Ain't it?

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:40.420
The secret is addin' a bit of
chili oil to the sesame dressin'.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:43.880
What's this?

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:44.900
Eggplant curry.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:48.760
The crisp texture and faint sweetness are perfect in curry!

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:55.020
And this ratatouille has such a full-bodied flavor it's hard to believe it's just vegetables.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:55.850
Seconds.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.480
Eat up, eat up!

00:04:58.480 --> 00:04:59.860
We got heaps to spare!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.580
What is it, Kousaku?

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.950
Kei, we've gained weight, haven't we?

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.080
You think so?

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:18.750
I'd say these are just muscles from all the harvesting work.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.550
Th-That's right!

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:24.420
I thought I was getting a bit round, but I'm sure it's just muscle!

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:27.720
Good work, Kou-tan, Kei!

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.100
Okay, that is <i>not</i> muscle!

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.900
We've become nothing more than fatties!

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.830
Yes... we have.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:45.320
Wha—Kou-tan, that ain't
no way to talk to a lady!

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:50.740
I bet you've convinced yourself you're just
"plus-size", "curvy", or a "BBW"!

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:52.700
So I'll tell it straight!

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.410
You're fatties!

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:05.760
He's right.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.540
You're lookin' flabby, Kinoshita-san.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.380
Well, <i>you're</i> pretty chubby yourself,

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:10.640
Mino-chubby!

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.510
This is your fault for
cooking so much good food.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:14.470
Wh-What?!

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:17.170
Well I ain't never
forced you to eat it!

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:18.140
Don't care!

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:30.200
Whoa! Every boy's dream
come true—a catfight!

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:33.330
Or not. More like sumo wrestling.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.160
Compared to the mud wresting incident, their movements are sloppier.

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:39.040
Because they gained weight so rapidly,

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:42.180
they've yet to learn how to take advantage of their size.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:43.210
I see.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.010
Can we just agree
to lose weight?!

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:55.430
We lost it.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:01.640
The key to losing weight is,
of course, exercise.

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:04.480
Luckily, we have plenty of
opportunities to exercise here.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.320
And what a relief that
Kinoshita-san's back to normal.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.240
Her history in the
entertainment industry shows.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:14.580
She has truly impressive self-discipline.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.870
It was Minori who had us the most worried.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:17.660
Worried?

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:18.700
Whatcha talkin' 'bout?

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.410
You know <i>exactly</i>
what I'm talking about.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:22.580
Look at this.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:29.260
<i>Who</i> was it who
stayed chubby the longest?

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:30.720
Who was it?

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:33.980
Who?!

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.550
<i>Lookit me!</i>

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:38.310
<i>I ain't never gonna get married now!</i>

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:40.350
<i>What do I do?!</i>

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:43.310
<i>Forget married. When's the baby due?</i>

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:45.360
<i>Waaaah!</i>

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:50.490
Now what would the Nakazawa family say if they saw you in this sorry state?

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:52.450
W-Well...

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:53.950
Whoops, I sent it.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.890
No! Lookit what you done did!

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.790
Hey! Cut that out!

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:03.500
Jerk! Scum! Maggot!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:04.580
Kousaku.

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.550
The soybeans...

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:13.880
There's this white, fuzzy stuff growing around the roots.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:16.470
It might be mold.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:21.470
You get mold pretty easily this time of year
if you water the crops too much.

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:23.600
I watered them every day.

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:25.600
Oh...

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:27.650
Every day.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:29.360
Through wind and rain.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:32.940
Um, you can probably skip
the watering when it rains.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.450
But if it's just mold,
that's no big deal.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:41.910
It'll go away in no time.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.500
How about we check up
on them during break time?

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:54.760
Let's see...

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:56.720
How's it look?

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:02.640
You've got to be kidding me...

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:08.270
Wh-What is it?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.900
Ringo, go get a teacher.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:17.160
Please.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.760
Southern blight.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.520
What's "southern blight"?

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.060
Is it a bad sickness?

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:49.730
It's a soil-transmitted disease.

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:54.570
Crops struck by southern blight
will eventually die.

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:58.110
The worst part is that it
forms sclerotia in the soil,

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.530
where the fungus can keep multiplying.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:01.440
What's that mean?

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:03.950
This disease contaminates the soil itself.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:07.250
How can we cure it?

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.870
We can't.

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:12.900
As long as the fungus remains,
it will attack again next season.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:17.400
The only way to control the infection is
to discard the soil and burn all the crops.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:18.630
That's horrible...

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:26.150
Talk about a bummer.

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:26.980
Indeed.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:32.980
Other schools who used the same supplier were also hit with the blight.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:36.320
If we had known earlier,
we could have preempted the problem.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.190
I see.

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:40.530
But it's not your fault at all.

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:44.980
Minori, how's Ringo doing?

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:46.950
She asked to be left alone for a spell.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:47.500
Has she eaten?

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:51.220
She said she would later, so I left her food.

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:52.210
Kousaku.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.590
Go talk to her.

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:57.140
Please.

00:10:57.140 --> 00:11:01.600
I reckon she'll listen to you, if anyone.

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:02.480
I'm not sure...

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:04.340
I know it!

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:05.970
Because she...

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.730
She needs your help, Kousaku.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:17.900
Ringo, can we talk?

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:28.160
Hey, I'm sure you know
how enjoyable agriculture can be.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:32.370
But despite that, fewer and fewer people are farming.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.250
If you ask me, it's because
it's not very rewarding.

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:40.420
You can work till you drop,
but that doesn't translate to more money.

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:47.280
There's no guarantee of a stable income.

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:48.470
In that case...

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.680
In that case, why farm at all?

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:53.940
I don't know.

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:58.520
I'm still looking for the answer myself.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:02.990
How'd it go?

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:04.680
Hard to say.

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:05.490
I see.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:07.700
This is not something she'll
come to terms with in a day.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.290
Kousaku.

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:17.080
Yeah?

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:21.640
I chose soybeans for Kinoshita's first field farming experience

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:27.430
partly in the hopes that
it would enrich her soul.

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:32.140
I thought perhaps they could change her,
the way they change the soil.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.140
Really?

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:38.520
I don't want her to regret
coming to Tamo Agricultural.

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:42.940
Kei.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:44.900
Yes?

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:49.330
I'm glad you're my best friend.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:51.490
Same to you.

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:52.910
Ooh, this is marvelous!

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:56.500
At a school already rich with flora, a forbidden friendship blossoms!

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:00.050
I'll title it Super Anal Brothers:
Enema Adventures!

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.460
We'll put out a
rush-printed book too!

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.220
That's 500 yen each.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:08.080
A wall table with the circle Franken should be 1,000 units easy.

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:09.760
Cha-ching, baby!

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:12.440
I'm back, against my better judgment.

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:15.350
I felt like that girl was calling for me.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:18.600
"We're finished" is what you should tell me when I act straight.

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:21.240
Now, you may as well just tell me to fap.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:22.400
Wh-What's the big idea?

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:25.400
Why are the Four Farm Deities all here?

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:27.280
What are these?

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:29.590
Payment for serving as inspiration.

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:31.530
Miso and a goldband lily?

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:33.700
Are these for Ringo?

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:35.200
I-It's not like—

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:38.180
It's not like we did this for
Kinoshita-san's sake or anything!

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:41.090
And it's not like we were too embarrassed to give it to her in person!

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:41.790
Kyaa!

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:44.960
Hey! Don't go stealing my lines like that!

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:49.300
That's the first time I've seen a macho <i>tsundere</i>.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:50.080
Kei.

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:54.100
I get the feeling Ringo's gonna be fine.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:55.560
After all...

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:57.310
Right.

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:21.080
Kousaku, you're awake?

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:22.290
This is bad.

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:23.630
Yeah.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.210
Let's wake Minori.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:25.880
Ringo too.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:32.950
I've contacted everyone in class who can reasonably come.

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:33.920
What's going on?

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:34.930
What are we here for?

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.430
To harvest the tomatoes.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:38.350
At this time of night?

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:40.600
We might already be too late.

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:41.800
Let's go.

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:42.900
O-Okay.

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:50.610
Look.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.450
They're torn open.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:56.410
You know how hot it's been lately?

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:59.040
Well, the tomatoes haven't been getting enough water.

00:14:59.590 --> 00:15:01.370
Then this storm comes.

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:03.380
The tomatoes absorb
so much water at once

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:04.960
that they split at the seams.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:06.670
Kamatori Kei!

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.800
Start from that row!

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:09.590
Got it.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.260
Worry about the split tomatoes later!

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:37.950
The damaged tomatoes

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.750
can be made into
purée, jam, or preserves.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.670
No need to waste 'em!

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.000
Why?

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.210
Why does no one look upset?

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:50.170
All that hard work to make
the tomatoes ready for harvest

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:52.340
just went to waste.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:54.300
Why does everyone accept it?

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.390
Hey, mind coming with me?

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:14.110
To you, this place is pretty rural, isn't it?

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:15.490
Yeah.

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.740
But it's a nice place.

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:19.490
There's so much nature.

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:19.990
Really?

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:27.460
But none of what you see
is truly untouched nature.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:30.460
The paddies and the fields,

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.340
the mountains, roads, and rivers...

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:36.300
have all been built up by humans over the generations.

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:41.520
Our predecessors faced a harsh and unforgiving wilderness.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:43.730
And it's not just here.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:48.310
All human settlements once bore witness to our clash with nature.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:50.150
They're battlefields.

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:50.860
Battlefields?

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:54.490
Agriculture can be trying sometimes,

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:59.620
but I'm sure you'll agree that watching crops grow is its own reward.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.330
I'm sure the people who sculpted this landscape felt the same way.

00:17:03.590 --> 00:17:06.370
They imagined what this town might become,

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:09.080
dreamed about us, their future generations,

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:11.750
and worked each day to make that a reality.

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:14.220
Who knows?

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:18.760
Maybe someone out there who's
encouraged by eating my vegetables

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:21.390
will go on to do great things.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:23.720
Even if they don't,

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:26.980
if I can give them the will
to face tomorrow head-on,

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:29.860
I'll have done my part for the future.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:33.820
I want to grow crops
with that kind of power.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:37.150
At the end of the day,
that's what keeps me farming.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:43.430
Sorry, I kinda started rambling.

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:44.620
Um, hey.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.920
You sent me vegetables, didn't you?

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:53.210
At the time, I was completely drained and had no appetite.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:57.050
That's when one of my staff made me a salad.

00:17:57.560 --> 00:18:00.510
He told me a fan had sent the ingredients.

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:04.970
I thought I owed it to that fan to eat it, so I forced myself to.

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:09.980
I was shocked.

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.680
It was like nothing I'd tasted before.

00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:12.710
The taste?

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:16.900
Earthy, a bit bitter, and a little tough,

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:18.700
but full of tenderness.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.950
I don't think I sent anything <i>that</i> special.

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.200
I knew.

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:27.200
It must have been the taste of life.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:29.960
The crops were sharing their life with me.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:33.420
Then, for some reason, I began to cry.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:36.440
I found I still had the will to go on.

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:39.300
As if someone was beside me, reassuring me.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:41.720
So you see...

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:49.190
I'm sure that's when...

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:55.360
After that, I made sure to eat everything you sent.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.320
I looked forward to reading your letters too.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:03.570
I've dreamed of coming to this school since we began exchanging letters.

00:19:03.880 --> 00:19:06.660
I was sure I'd enjoy it here.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:07.950
Hang on a sec.

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:11.170
I never sent any letters.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:14.750
But you mailed me vegetables, didn't you?

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:16.380
Yeah.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.380
But I didn't write my name.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:19.590
Nor any letters.

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:24.350
But they were signed by you.

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:26.390
You were in the photographs too.

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:27.560
Photographs?

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:31.640
This picture...

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:33.560
Do you have the letters too?

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:46.000
We're finally done!

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:48.410
I'll fix dinner right away.

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:53.160
What's gotten you lookin' so solemn?

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:53.920
Did something happen?

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:56.660
There's something I'd like you to see.

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:01.560
You recognize these, don't you,

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:02.420
Minori?

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:05.560
Why did you do this?

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:10.310
Sending letters to Ringo—
to Kusakabe Yuka under my name!

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:11.930
Shucks, you found out?

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:16.200
I was makin' sure you didn't
come across too creepy!

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:17.330
Got a problem with that?

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:21.030
Er, uh...

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.110
Now that you mention it, no.

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:26.610
Honest, sendin' a package without so much as a howdy-do?

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:28.550
They woulda thrown it right out!

00:20:28.550 --> 00:20:30.240
Okay, okay, but wait!

00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:34.120
How's Ringo supposed to feel,
having read your letters thinking they were mine?

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:37.460
You're right.

00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:42.300
I'm sorry, Kinoshita-san.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:47.050
I wrote as honestly as I could 'bout all that was said or done at school.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.680
Still, I'm sorry.

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:53.680
Look up.

00:20:58.270 --> 00:20:59.820
You were the one.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:04.600
I've been longing to meet you.

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:06.160
Wait—Kinoshita-san...

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:09.410
I've wanted to meet and
talk to you for so long.

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:14.660
What you wrote about
your school and agriculture

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:18.040
has filled my dreams ever since.

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:19.040
You ain't angry?

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:21.460
Why would I be?

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:24.630
Well, I lied and pretended to be Kousaku.

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:27.800
But what you wrote in your letters was all true.

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:32.180
Besides, I never told you the truth either.

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:33.470
So, you see?

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:35.220
We're even.

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:36.690
I see.

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:39.230
We ain't all that different.

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.190
Yeah.

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:45.990
Hey, can I call you Mino-poyo?

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:47.040
Sure thing!

00:21:47.040 --> 00:21:49.650
Do I get to call you Ringo-cchi in return?

00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:50.490
I'd love that!

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:53.490
Mino-poyo, I love you!

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:55.960
Well, isn't this grand?

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:59.170
Ringo's cheered up, and all the mysteries have been solved.

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:01.130
For the most part, a happy ending!

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:02.500
Like hell it is!

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:06.010
This just can't be right!

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:39.640
"Cooking Cougar".
